From d7d24906ca42a56f763910d3bb651488c1ee7890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:57:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] nv50: size surface views by blocks when the block size
 differs

The VA frontend clears YUYV and UYVY video buffers, whose R8G8_R8B8 and
G8R8_B8R8 resources hold two pixels per block, through RGBA8 surfaces.
nv50_surface_from_miptree takes the surface size from the resource in
pixels, so the render target comes out twice as wide as the buffer.
Since clears no longer read their surface templates as nv50_surface,
they cover the whole render target and write past the end of the
buffer: RT_FAULT traps with PAGE_NOT_PRESENT whenever a program creates
such a surface, as mpv does when it probes formats.

Convert the size to blocks of the view format when the block sizes
differ, as radeonsi does.

Tested on a GeForce GT 240M: with the previous patches, uploading a
YUYV or UYVY frame through VA left 3 RT_FAULT lines in the kernel log,
starting mpv --hwdec=vaapi 6, and mpv --vo=dmabuf-wayland 54. With this
patch there are none, and the uploaded frames still read back
unchanged.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_miptree.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_miptree.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_miptree.c
index 3cb093a..faf30cc 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_miptree.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_miptree.c
@@ -485,6 +485,19 @@ nv50_surface_from_miptree(struct nv50_miptree *mt,
    ns->depth = ps->last_layer - ps->first_layer + 1;
    ns->offset = mt->level[templ->level].offset;
 
+   /* A view in a format with another block size, such as RGBA8 on a
+    * subsampled R8G8_R8B8 video buffer, covers the same blocks.
+    */
+   if (util_format_get_blockwidth(ps->format) !=
+       util_format_get_blockwidth(mt->base.base.format) ||
+       util_format_get_blockheight(ps->format) !=
+       util_format_get_blockheight(mt->base.base.format)) {
+      ns->width = util_format_get_nblocksx(mt->base.base.format, ns->width) *
+                  util_format_get_blockwidth(ps->format);
+      ns->height = util_format_get_nblocksy(mt->base.base.format, ns->height) *
+                   util_format_get_blockheight(ps->format);
+   }
+
    ns->width <<= mt->ms_x;
    ns->height <<= mt->ms_y;
 
